<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The status-bar and notification icon.

  Separate from `ic_launcher` on purpose, and not optional: Android draws a
  small icon from its **alpha channel only**, tinted a flat colour. The
  launcher icon is an adaptive icon whose background layer is an opaque square,
  so passing it here renders a solid blob — which is what
  `applicationInfo.icon` produced: a filled circle with no mark in it,
  identical to every other app's fallback.

  So the rules are different from the launcher's. Transparent everywhere except
  the mark, no background layer, no colour of its own, and sized 24dp rather
  than 108dp with a safe zone — the whole canvas is usable and the mark should
  nearly fill it, because it is drawn at status-bar size.

  Placeholder mark, same H as `ic_launcher_foreground`. Replace both together
  when the real Homerun mark lands.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M4.75,2 h4.545 v7.727 h5.455 v-7.727 h4.545 v20 h-4.545 v-7.727 h-5.455 v7.727 h-4.545 z" />
</vector>
